            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>An apparatus that displays synthetic scene images for augmented reality, virtual reality and other display types. One or more pairs of input beams (70, 76) are injected into a display panel incorporating a layer (100) of nonlinear optical (NLO) material. The input beams are brought to cross each other in the NLO material in a noncollinear geometry where a product beam (82) of a sum frequency equal to the sum of the frequencies of the input beams (70, 76) is generated by sum frequency generation and directed to the eye (160) of a viewer. The synthetic scene image information is impressed on each input beam pair by amplitude and phase modulation to set the amplitude (i.e. brightness), wavevector (i.e. direction) and wavefront radius of curvature (i.e. depth) of the synthetic scene image. For colour display, three pairs of input beams with respective sum frequencies in three primary colours are used.</p>
            </abstract>
